// Article 3. Incapacity and who the trustee is.
#require "1-creation.charter".
Fact physician
Fact certified Identified by physician
Act certify-incapacity Actor physician Creates certified(physician)
Bool incapacitated
  Holds when Count(Foreach physician: physician When certified(physician)) >= 2

Var successor Identified by person
Fact trustee Identified by person
  Default settlor-is-trustee Holds when person == Margaret
  Exception settlor-cannot-act Overrides settlor-is-trustee
    Rejects when person == Margaret && (incapacitated() || deceased(Margaret))
  Default successor-steps-in
    Holds when successor(person) && (incapacitated() || deceased(Margaret))

Clause 3.1 Approved "41eb4d22a0de578d4874691e57930c933fc210b23ea4163a7dcf0eed85db7aff"
  Norm "The settlor is incapacitated when two physicians certify in writing that she cannot manage her affairs." => certify-incapacity
Clause 3.2 Approved "72b14930871018e5aa065a1184e8b3177484e1574a5db4f606891e8f1a98b144"
  Definition "While the settlor is incapacitated, and after her death, the successor trustee acts as trustee. The first successor trustee is Daniel Ellis."
.
+successor(Daniel).
